-- title:
--   First Switcheroo Error Le Eighth Stage
-- statement:
--   **The first switcheroo error is bounded by the explicit eighth-power envelope.**
--
--   Assume $\gamma\ge0$, $\zeta\ge0$, $\zeta\le1$, and $d\le q$. Form the switcheroo error with both self-consistency inputs equal to $\zeta$, and use the main commutativity error at parameters $\gamma$ and $\zeta$. Then
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{sw}}\left(\zeta,\zeta;E_{\mathrm{main}}(\gamma,\zeta)\right)
--   \le
--   36m\left(\operatorname{rpow}(\gamma,1/8)+\operatorname{rpow}(\zeta,1/8)+\operatorname{rpow}(d/q,1/8)\right).
--   $$
--
--   The estimate is the first scalar switcheroo bound in the complete-part commutation proof. The three terms measure the main commutativity error, the slice self-consistency error, and the degree-to-field-size ratio after taking eighth roots.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.firstSwitcherooError_le_eighth_stage`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
